    "summary": "High‑energy backyard set with scorching Hard To Handle and epic The Other One",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a blistering Hard To Handle, a soaring The Other One suite and a heartfelt Wharf Rat. Jerry’s crystal‑clear guitar and Pigpen’s electric piano texture shine, while Bill Kreutzmann provides powerhouse drumming. Overall the performance is high‑energy with strong transitions throughout.",
    "review": "June 21, 1971 at the Chateau d'HerouvilIe finds the Dead in top form during an intimate French backyard gig. From the opening Truckin' through a rollicking run of covers and originals, the band never loses its momentum – the set is punctuated by a scorching Hard To Handle that showcases Jerry’s crystalline lead work, a tightly woven China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue, and an expansive The Other One → Wharf Rat stretch driven by Bill Kreutzmann’s thunderous drumming. Pigpen’s electric piano adds a rare 1971 texture, especially on the soulful Morning Dew, while the high‑octane Black Peter and raucous Johnny B. Goode close the night with pure excitement. The Miller soundboard capture is exceptional, offering crisp separation that lets every nuance of the performance shine.",
